{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789956438,"nonce":"/A+FLtox/B8e8siB0K/b3/pXiy0=","title":"haxe.Template took the wrong branch: anon shapes conflated field types, `var x;` was typed by `x = null`, and Dynamic arithmetic added box addresses","message":"Found while retrying callee-first method lowering (400d468): with\n`makeExpr` typed `Void-\u003eDynamic`, `::if (n \u003e 2)::` for n = 1 produced\nneither branch, and `::if isMale::` with a false field printed the if\nbranch on HEAD as well (Issue8560). Three defects under it, none about\nTemplate:\n\n1. An anonymous structure's runtime shape id hashed only the sorted field\n   NAMES, and the runtime keeps the first descriptor registered under an\n   id, so `{n: 5}` after `{n: true}` read its field as Bool\n   (`Reflect.getProperty({n: 5}, \"n\")` printed `true`). The id now hashes\n   the descriptor, names with their runtime types (literals.rs, anon.rs).\n\n2. `var eelse;` followed by `eelse = null;` in one branch and\n   `eelse = parseBlock(tokens);` in another was typed Dynamic at the first\n   assignment and never revisited; the enum then boxed on the way into the\n   local and `run(eelse)` switched on a box. A null-initialised local now\n   waits for the first assignment that carries a type.\n\n3. `a \u003e b` and `a + b` on two Dynamic locals whose boxes came from a typed\n   `Void-\u003eDynamic` call compared and added the box ADDRESSES; only locals\n   initialised from a literal were tracked as boxes. Two pointer-shaped\n   Dynamic operands now go through `haxe_dynamic_arith` / `haxe_dynamic_order`,\n   which read each side as the box it is or the raw slot it is (a String\n   on either side of `+` concatenates; two integral operands stay Int), and\n   a binding initialised from a known box is tracked as one.\n\nWith these, callee-first method body lowering lands: a caller declared\nabove a method whose return type is inferred sees that type\n(`cat(\"x\") != \"ax\"` — 400d468). Two follow-ons the gate demanded: a read\nof a binding tracked as a box marks its register as one (Issue3447: a\nFloat box reached `eq`'s erased slot through `haxe_unbox_scalar_or_addr`,\nwhich keeps a non-Int box's ADDRESS), and a binding typed as a structure\nbut initialised from a known box keeps reading its fields by name\n(Issue9590: a parsed JSON object is Map-backed, so an index read gives 0).\nA parameter stored into an element of this class's array field takes the\nelement type (Issue5477 moved from CRASH to a wrong evaluation order).\n\nProbes: TP2, TP8 (Template, match `haxe --run`), DC1/DC3, RG1.","files":null}]}